	(text "Oil-temperature gauge front end, option A (minimal). Two copper layers, through-hole parts only. J1 takes the display lead (3.3 V, SDA, SCL,\neach paired with a ground); the display runs from its own USB-C socket. J2 takes the sender harness."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "00f15780-0a28-52e3-a2ea-b9cef3bedd4e")
	)
	(text "Layout rules: AIN1, AIN2, SENDER and SENSE keep at least 1 mm from ground copper, and there is no\nground pour (a short there gives a believable wrong reading). R1 meets SENDER at J2 pin 1 by its own\ntrack. J2 pin 3 is empty, between the sense wire and the return."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 43.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "461190f1-0aa0-50c0-a62b-e1140fff03e6")
	)
	(text "Measurement (hardware/WIRING.md): the ADC drives 250 uA out of A0 through Rref and the sender.\nVref = A0 - A1 across Rref, Vs = A1 - A2 across the sender, Rs = Rref x Vs / Vref.\nR1 and R2 tap the sender and the ground-sense wire; at least 2 kOhm between every harness wire and the ADC."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dab437bb-cf1a-54f6-b0fd-50665211c921")
	)
